00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:45.300
The theme for this
year's breakfast

00:12:45.300 --> 00:12:48.480
is maximizing potential,
the congruence

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:51.360
of diversity and excellence.

00:12:51.360 --> 00:12:53.820
By choosing this
theme, the committee

00:12:53.820 --> 00:12:58.020
aims to showcase how and
why diversity enriches

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:02.640
the research, academic, and
community triad that embodies

00:13:02.640 --> 00:13:05.630
MIT's mission and focus.

00:13:05.630 --> 00:13:08.090
We'll begin this morning's
program with an invocation

00:13:08.090 --> 00:13:10.400
from Reverend Robert Randolph.

00:13:10.400 --> 00:13:13.550
Following the invocation, we
will have breakfast and then

00:13:13.550 --> 00:13:16.520
resume the program with
a musical selection.

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.920
Now let us receive the
Chaplain to the Institute,

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:21.578
Reverend Robert Randolph, who
will offer the invocation.

00:13:21.578 --> 00:13:24.566
[APPLAUSE]

00:13:32.040 --> 00:13:34.260
RANDOLPH: It is always
good to precede breakfast.

00:13:38.260 --> 00:13:39.820
Let us pray together.

00:13:43.440 --> 00:13:46.770
Almighty God, we ask
your presence with us

00:13:46.770 --> 00:13:50.550
on this day when we
remember your servant,

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:54.790
Martin Luther King,
Jr. We remember

00:13:54.790 --> 00:14:00.730
that he challenged us to make
real the promises of America.

00:14:00.730 --> 00:14:05.890
And we confess that we
have not always done so.

00:14:05.890 --> 00:14:08.980
We have made progress,
but we have far

00:14:08.980 --> 00:14:12.360
to go before justice
is established,

00:14:12.360 --> 00:14:16.850
and mercy flows
like living water.

00:14:16.850 --> 00:14:24.110
We are reminded of our failures
by our brother, James Shirley.

00:14:24.110 --> 00:14:28.210
We give thanks for
his courage and pray

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:32.030
that his witness will
sharpen our commitment

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:38.080
to deal with the racism
that too often confronts us.

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:41.980
Give us wisdom as
we respond to James.

00:14:41.980 --> 00:14:45.040
Give him strength,
and give us strength

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:48.760
as we seek together to
grapple with the scourge

00:14:48.760 --> 00:14:49.535
that we confront.

00:14:52.410 --> 00:14:56.740
And we pray that you will
be present with us today,

00:14:56.740 --> 00:15:00.320
that we may learn
from one another

00:15:00.320 --> 00:15:05.540
and leave this place
committed anew to the notion

00:15:05.540 --> 00:15:11.400
that it is not what we know,
but who we are that will

00:15:11.400 --> 00:15:15.500
make a difference in our world.

00:15:15.500 --> 00:15:20.780
Hear our prayer, Almighty
God, and let the congregation

00:15:20.780 --> 00:15:22.665
say, Amen.

